er classified information so  nothing to be seen here nothing to be  investigated well you may be shocked to  learn that this is not actually how the  process works presidents do have the  ability to declassify certain types of  information but there's a procedure  attached to it certain executive branch  officials have the authority to deem  information as confidential secret or  top secret and if it's ultra top secret  then the document will get the sci  designation some of the documents in  donald trump's possession had this very  distinction there are also rules  limiting how the documents can be stored  physically transported or electronically  transmitted when someone with the proper  authority moves to declassify the  documents the executive branch has a  process to involve the other agencies  that might be affected and certainly the  president is one of the people who can  move to make something declassified it's  rarely done but it can happen however  they need to undergo this very same  process and it's not as easy as made  waving a magic wand as cash patel would  have you believe here's former cia  director and former defense secretary  leon panetta who would know a thing or  two about this very topic being even  more frank than i have been about the  process for how to declassify documents  so you're obviously very well versed in  dealing with classified material former  trump aides are now trying to claim that  there was a standing order by the  president donald trump to declassify any  document that left the west wing for  trump's resident  is that how declassification works  even with some of the nation's most  guarded secrets  uh you know that's nonsense and uh and  he knows it  uh the reality is that there is a  process  for declassifying information  uh and presidents want to declassify  they have to follow that process which  basically requires that it be referred  to the agencies that are responsible for  classifying that material they have  something to say as to whether or not  that material should be declassified so  there is  nothing  that i'm aware of  that indicates that a formal step was  taken by this president to in fact  declassify anything right now this is  pretty much bs it's all a bunch of bs  says leon panetta and then there's an  added layer of security when you're  talking about nuclear documents which  donald trump is accused of having in his  possession as documents about nuclear  material are subject to the atomic  energy act which the president does not  have unilateral authority over now  secondary to this entire discussion is  that even if the documents weren't  classified or even if they were deemed  declassified by donald trump right  before he left office with his magic  wand it wouldn't serve to get the former  president out of hot water because none  of the things that donald trump is being  investigated for require the documents  be  classified the espionage act violations  concealing documents and obstruction of  justice are the three things that the  fbi is looking into as it pertains to  donald trump those are not dependent on  whether the information that trump had  in his possession were classified he's  not supposed to be taking hiding or  destroying any of the presidential  records regardless of their  classification status and the government  asked him to return the items he didn't  willingly hand them over he didn't give  back all of the documents anyway and so  it doesn't matter whether or not they  were classified final point on this  because the right has been talking  non-stop about hillary clinton and her  emails over the past couple of weeks  they used to say that hillary clinton  she could not be trusted to handle  secret information therefore she could  not be president because when she was  secretary of state she had uh secret  documents in her gmail account that was  being operated through a private server  and it was grossly negligent we just  can't trust her with these top secret  documents well if that was ever your  concern  but you also now have this position that  the president can just declassify  whatever they want on a whim doesn't  this render the point that they were  making about hillary in 2016 completely  moot like why would it matter that  hillary clinton supposedly uh wasn't  able to be trusted with classified  information if she would have the power  as president to just declassify whatever  she wants anyway but the contradictions  we know when it comes to the right wing  they don't matter it's all about  twisting and turning yourself anything  that you can do to defend donald trump  no matter how ridiculous it makes you  look
 

